node_modules
.env
.openzeppelin

#Hardhat files
cache
artifacts

# Editors
.idea/**

# Safe operations.
#
# The bundle itself (safe-bundles/<name>.json) IS committed: it is the record
# of exactly what was authorized, authorizes nothing on its own, and is
# derivable from public chain state. Co-signers can pull it rather than being
# emailed a file, and it is no longer at risk from `git clean -fdx`.
#
# Signature material is NEVER committed. A set of `threshold` signatures is a
# bearer authorization -- anyone holding it can execute the transaction. This
# matters far more for future bundles (sweepAll, pause) than for an
# acceptOwnership batch, so the rule is unconditional. Signatures live in
# per-signer sidecars, which stay local.
safe-bundles/*/signatures-*.json
# Generated artifacts, all reproducible from the bundle with
# `safe:sign-page` / `safe:build`.
safe-bundles/*/sign.html
safe-bundles/*/tx-builder/
safe-bundles/*/eip712/
